## Inspect before changing

Start by checking the active account and workspace. Inspect existing resources before creating replacements. The resource returned by a previous operation is usually more useful than a guessed name.

## Capture identifiers

When a command returns a resource or operation identifier, store it for the next step. Prefer JSON output to a script that extracts values from a status sentence.

```bash
miosa capabilities --json
miosa app inspect ./app --json
miosa app plan ./app --goal deploy --json
```

## Read failures as state

An interrupted client does not necessarily mean the server operation stopped. Inspect the recorded operation before retrying it. A retry must not silently create a second resource.

## Choose the interface

Use the CLI for terminal work, the [SDKs](/docs/sdks) for application code, and [MCP](/docs/mcp) for a client that needs a tool interface.
